                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I recommend this game, but look at the store page and realize you get what is advertised. For those down voting because this game isn't like King's Bounty I don't understand why you would think it was. This is a very basic, simple, easy to navigate game with the barest similarity to King's Bounty. The nice thing is that the combats are quick. I LOVED King's Bounty but some of those combats could take quite a long time and that game was definitely advertised as a much longer experience.\r\n\r\nI played this before Beasts Battle and after starting that game, I can see some definite improvements in this sequel (renamed Necromancer Returns). There is a massive difficulty spike at the very end with the last few battles being pretty difficult. I barely beat the last battle after several tries. I had trouble with two Achievements based entirely on how they are worded in the Achievement descriptions. I made a post in the Discussions for this game in case it helps anyone else.\r\n\r\nThis isn't a game I would play more than once, but it was a fun experience and doesn't require a lot of concentration. I like that there are battles that can be repeated for grinding, but there is a cap on XP so grinding isn't really necessary. You earn enough XP to get all the spells, skills, and upgrade all the units and get all those associated Achievements but then the XP stops accumulating no matter how many battles you do after the cap. And I never made enough money to get all the best equipment, but that was probably because in the beginning I didn't pay close enough attention to how many units I was losing (they are automatically replaced at the end of each battle by lowering your gold earned) and I didn't prioritize getting the skill for increased gold because I honestly lost track and didn't see that I didn't select that until I only had a few skills left to choose from.\r\n\r\nWith this game you get what you pay for and what the store page advertises. There isn't a deep story or character development or anything like that. It is purely a short game about basic strategy in battles. I enjoyed my experience and if you like these kinds of simpler games I recommend getting it on sale. Without any grinding and without trying to experiment with getting the last two Achievements I probably would have finished this game in about 10 hours or so. It is a very easy game to play a little at a time and pick right back up again.",
